{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Praise Him, all His angels</b> — these are the non-corporeal ones." "<b>And then all His hosts</b> — and these are pure bodies, not composite, and they are the many stars that are in the sphere of the zodiac. And afterward he mentioned the attendants, and he mentioned first sun and moon, for they are the rulers, and afterward he mentioned all stars of light, because they have great light because of their being close to the earth. And afterward he mentioned the heavens of the heaven, and it is the sphere of fire that is adjacent to the sphere of the moon. And afterward he mentioned the sphere of the zodiac [lit. sphere of Sagittarius] and the waters that are above the heavens — thus far is the boundary of the upper world. And behold, he began with the noble and concluded with the lowly, and the opposite of this he did in mentioning the lower world. And he said of the upper world: <i>those who dwell in it praise</i> [yehallelu]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:07.055217643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}